# Fixed npm-tree rows (undici, brace-expansion, ip-address, tar) and re2js
# are dropped on purpose: pm's npm is 12.2.2, which bundles fixed copies,
# and the Dockerfile assembler replaces the npm inside the Node tarball with
# that tree. markdownlint-cli2 0.24.1 pulls re2js 2.9.1. A later copy of any
# of them in the image must fail the release scan. Repo lockfiles (pnpm,
# clickup-mcp, photon sidecar) carry none of these versions (trivy fs,
# 2026-11-15).
#
# Residual CVE-2026-78661 (golang.org/x/net fix 0.62.0) in op and gh, and
# CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools 70.3.0 vendored in pip/_vendor), are skipped by
# the release scan (--skip-files, --skip-dirs) and tracked in the monolith
# supply-chain ignore rows, not here.

# zod (CVE-2023-54404, denial of service on unbounded array validation).
# The photon sidecar is on zod 4.6.7 (fixed). clickup-mcp zod 3.25.76: clickup-mcp 1.8.0 and the latest 1.9.0 require
# zod ^3.24.2 and the fix exists only in zod 4, a major the server is not
# written for, so an override would break it. It validates tool arguments
# from Sera's own model over stdio, not inbound messages. Re-check then.
# Re-checked 2026-11-09: Trivy no longer flags zod 3.25.76 (GHSA still lists
# < 4.6.6); kept dated to 2026-12-01 in case the DB is corrected.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-12-01
